---
import { scryerPreview } from "../data/scryer-preview";
---

<section class="scryer-access" id="scryer-access" aria-labelledby="scryer-access-title">
  <div class="access-header">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Scryer, served by Stithy · public research access</p>
      <h3 id="scryer-access-title">Try Scryer</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="version-status" aria-label="Released Scryer tool version">
      <span class="version-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span id="scryer-live-version" aria-live="polite">checking live version</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="access-intro">One MCP endpoint, two scoped research keys. Both can call the full <code>wolf.scryer.*</code> tool family. Pick based on what you're willing to share, not on whether your question counts.</p>
  <div class="access-tiers">
    <div class="access-tier">
      <div class="tier-heading"><h4>Base</h4><span class="tier-tag">question text not kept</span></div>
      <p>Full maths surface. Calls are counted and timed, but your question is not stored. A 30-second deadline and shared compute budget.</p>
      <div class="credential"><code id="scryer-base-key">{scryerPreview.baseKey}</code><button type="button" class="copy-key" data-key="scryer-base-key" aria-label="Copy base research bearer token">Copy</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="access-tier contributor">
      <div class="tier-heading"><h4>Contributor</h4><span class="tier-tag">question text kept</span></div>
      <p>Your full input is recorded to help improve the engine. In exchange: a 120-second deadline, more memory, and a higher queue priority.</p>
      <div class="credential"><code id="scryer-contributor-key">{scryerPreview.contributorKey}</code><button type="button" class="copy-key" data-key="scryer-contributor-key" aria-label="Copy contributor research bearer token">Copy</button></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="warning">These keys may stop working at any time due to abuse.</p>
  <p class="access-foot">Use <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;key&gt;</code> with <a href={scryerPreview.endpoint} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the MCP endpoint</a>. Read the <a href={scryerPreview.docs} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">live tool docs</a> with the same header. Neither tier logs IP addresses; both log call timing and tool/outcome metadata. The version above is fetched from the live docs, not baked into this page. Docs and MCP links require the bearer header; an anonymous browser visit returns 401.</p>
</section>

<style>
  .scryer-access { grid-column: 1 / -1; min-width: 0; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / .13); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: clamp(1rem, 2.4vw, 1.5rem); padding-bottom: clamp(1.4rem, 2.7vw, 1.7rem); background: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / .025); }
  .access-header { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: space-between; gap: .8rem 1.2rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: .65rem; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: .55; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 .25rem; }
  h3 { font-size: 1.06rem; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.25; margin: 0; }
  .version-status { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .44rem; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / .12); border-radius: 999px; padding: .3rem .65rem; font-size: .72rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; opacity: .8; white-space: nowrap; }
  .version-dot { width: .37rem; height: .37rem; border-radius: 50%; background: currentColor; opacity: .55; }
  .version-status[data-live] .version-dot { background: #57c8ad; opacity: 1; }
  .access-intro { font-size: .84rem; line-height: 1.55; opacity: .72; margin: .85rem 0 1.05rem; max-width: 70ch; }
  .access-tiers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .7rem; }
  .access-tier { min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .55rem; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / .11); border-radius: .7rem; padding: .85rem; background: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / .025); }
  .access-tier.contributor { border-color: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / .18); }
  .tier-heading { display: flex; gap: .35rem .65rem; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  h4 { margin: 0; font-size: .88rem; font-weight: 650; }
  .tier-tag { font-size: .73rem; opacity: .72; }
  .access-tier p { font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.55; opacity: .74; margin: 0; flex: 1; }
  .credential { display: flex; align-items: stretch; gap: .4rem; min-width: 0; margin-top: .25rem; }
  .credential code { min-width: 0; flex: 1; padding: .48rem .55rem; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / .09); border-radius: .4rem; background: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / .04); font: .7rem/1.45 ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace; overflow-wrap: anywhere; user-select: all; }
  .copy-key { align-self: stretch; padding: .3rem .55rem; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / .2); border-radius: .4rem; background: transparent; color: inherit; cursor: pointer; font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3; font-family: inherit; min-width: 3.7rem; }
  .copy-key:hover, .copy-key:focus-visible { background: rgb(var(--color-text-rgb) / .1); }
  .copy-key:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 2px; }
  .warning { display: inline-block; margin: 1.2rem 0 .7rem; color: #ead5d8; font-size: .79rem; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.5; letter-spacing: .01em; text-shadow: -1px 0 rgba(255,70,102,.55), 1px 0 rgba(57,215,246,.55); }
  .access-foot { margin: 0; font-size: .78rem; line-height: 1.55; opacity: .72; }
  .access-foot a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .access-tiers { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
</style>

<script>
  function bootScryerAccess() {
    const version = document.getElementById('scryer-live-version');
    const base = document.getElementById('scryer-base-key');
    if (!version || !base) return;
    const holder = version.closest<HTMLElement>('.version-status');
    const token = base.textContent?.trim();
    if (!token) { version.textContent = 'version unavailable'; return; }
    const controller = new AbortController();
    const timeout = window.setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 7000);
    fetch('https://mcp.woflo.dev/stithy/docs', {
      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` },
      signal: controller.signal,
      cache: 'no-store',
    }).then(async response => {
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Live docs unavailable');
      const text = await response.text();
      const rows = [...text.matchAll(/^\|\s*\[`wolf\.scryer\.(?:ask|check|verify)`\]\([^)]+\)\s*\|\s*(\d+\.\d+\.\d+(?:[-+][\w.-]+)?)\s*\|/gm)];
      const versions = new Set(rows.map(row => row[1]));
      if (rows.length !== 3 || versions.size !== 1) throw new Error('Scryer release versions disagree');
      version.textContent = `Scryer v${rows[0][1]}`;
      holder?.setAttribute('data-live', '');
      holder?.setAttribute('title', 'Live released version of ask, check and verify');
    }).catch(() => { version.textContent = 'version unavailable'; })
      .finally(() => window.clearTimeout(timeout));

    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.copy-key').forEach(button => {
      button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const key = document.getElementById(button.dataset.key || '')?.textContent?.trim();
        if (!key) return;
        try {
          if (navigator.clipboard && window.isSecureContext) {
            await navigator.clipboard.writeText(key);
          } else {
            const field = document.createElement('textarea');
            field.value = key;
            field.style.position = 'fixed';
            field.style.opacity = '0';
            document.body.appendChild(field);
            field.select();
            const copied = document.execCommand('copy');
            field.remove();
            if (!copied) throw new Error('Copy unavailable');
          }
          button.textContent = 'Copied';
        } catch {
          button.textContent = 'Select key';
          const range = document.createRange();
          const node = document.getElementById(button.dataset.key || '');
          if (node) { range.selectNodeContents(node); window.getSelection()?.removeAllRanges(); window.getSelection()?.addRange(range); }
        }
        window.setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 2000);
      });
    });
  }
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', bootScryerAccess);
</script>
